{"text": " You wake up in 1884 at Shinagawa on Tokyo Bay. A training ship called the Tsukuba is getting ready to sail. Did you know that on a voyage like this one, the year before, almost half the crew got sick from what they ate? On the ship Ryujo, 169 men got Barry-Barry. 25 died. Here's a sailor's plate, white rice, rice was free. Everything else cost money. A navy doctor, Takaki Kanahiro, measures what the men eat and changes the menu. More barley, meat, milk, bread, and vegetables. On the Tsukuba, 14 men get sick, none die. And the 14, they had not eaten the new food. So what is food now? Something to measure. What's inside it matters? Japan's first life tables give a newborn about 43 years. And Japanese men born back then, about 15 centimeter shorter than men born a century later. Decades later, it gets a name of vitamin. But knowing what's missing doesn't put it on a poor family's plate.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 3.98, "text": " You wake up in 1884 at Shinagawa on Tokyo Bay.", "tokens": [50364, 509, 6634, 493, 294, 2443, 25494, 412, 17347, 559, 10449, 322, 15147, 7840, 13, 50606], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19027054222830891, "compression_ratio": 1.4896551724137932, "no_speech_prob": 0.013399788178503513, "words": [{"word": " You", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.14, "probability": 0.726738691329956}, {"word": " wake", "start": 0.14, "end": 0.3, "probability": 0.9760338664054871}, {"word": " up", "start": 0.3, "end": 0.48, "probability": 0.9988068342208862}, {"word": " in", "start": 0.48, "end": 0.6, "probability": 0.9954044818878174}, {"word": " 1884", "start": 0.6, "end": 1.42, "probability": 0.9918802082538605}, {"word": " at", "start": 1.42, "end": 2.16, "probability": 0.897261381149292}, {"word": " Shinagawa", "start": 2.16, "end": 2.82, "probability": 0.6914534767468771}, {"word": " on", "start": 2.82, "end": 3.38, "probability": 0.7689108848571777}, {"word": " Tokyo", "start": 3.38, "end": 3.72, "probability": 0.9198620